Comment:
How to make the argument for electric cars:
1) Start with a trite and historically inaccurate cliche about the transition from horses to automobiles;
2) Go downhill from there.

Some important corrections: 
- truck has 200-300 gal tanks, it is much more than 500lbs (1500-2000lbs for fuel alone);
- weight of engine doesn't include oil, coolant, intake and exhaust (DEF system alone is around 1000lbs);
- modern trucks are not modern actually, they do have new engines, but cabin, frame and other parts are actually very old tech, so heavy, not safe and not efficient. They are made in an old school way and we know what Tesla does the best - manufacturing!
I wouldn't be surprised if Tesla Semi could haul 45-48k lbs of actual load, like all other trucks.

